  "headline": "City of Joy",
  "short_description": "Kolkata's colonial architecture, literary heritage and passionate cultural life make it India's intellectual and artistic capital.",
  "about": "The former capital of British India, Kolkata (Calcutta) remains a centre of literature, art, cinema and political thought, on the banks of the Hooghly river.\n\nLocated on the eastern bank of the Hooghly river (a Ganga distributary) in West Bengal.\n\nRenowned for Bengali literature, Rabindra Sangeet music, art and its Durga Puja celebrations.\n\nPredominantly Hindu, with significant Muslim, Christian, Sikh and Jewish minority heritage.",
  "history": "Founded as a British East India Company trading post in the late 17th century and the capital of British India until 1911.",
  "history_verified": false,
  "transportation": "- Netaji Subhas Chandra Bose International Airport (airport)\n- Howrah Junction (railway)\n- Esplanade Bus Terminus (bus terminal)",
  "travel_info": "Languages: Bengali, Hindi, English\nBudget: mid range",
  "best_time_text": "October to March",
  "ideal_duration_text": "2–3 days",
